<title>UK: British blue chips' drop ranks among biggest falls.</title>
<headline>British blue chips' drop ranks among biggest falls.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The FTSE 100 index's 2.5 percent drop on Friday marked the biggest percentage fall in Britain's leading share index since October 1992.</p>
<p>Here is a list of the FTSE 100's largest falls, in numerical and percentage terms, in its 14 year history</p>
<p>1) &quot;The Crash&quot; -- 250.7 points, or 12.22 percent, on October 20, 1987</p>
<p>2) 249.6 points, or 10.84 percent, on October 19, 1987</p>
<p>3) 111.1 points, or 6.19 percent, on October 26, 1987</p>
<p>4) 110.6 points, or 5.69 percent, on October 22, 1987</p>
<p>5) 103.4 points, or 4.06 percent, on October 5, 1992</p>
<p>6) 125.5 points, or 2.51 percent, on August 15, 1997</p>
